iterations.reply:
The http-client import and the enrichment fetch are removed. The node's `with` clause grants only `LLMClient<inference>`, and the linker enforces that clause regardless of the approval. To add the fetch, the platform team needs to add `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` to `ParseMessage`'s `with` clause in the graph, then regenerate the node. The node's output is the same as before, because the fetch never affected it.

The fetch also needs a second look before it's re-added. It would put the raw, untrusted message text into an outbound URL, sending up to 4000 characters of user input to another host. As written, the code also doesn't percent-encode the text.

